# Burden of Proof on Bot1's own Detective (Novice Inspector, 1/2): "as long as it's a Detective you control" holds, so it gets +2/+2 (3/4) and the
# "otherwise" half (base 1/1, can't block Detectives) is off. It blocks Bot2's Novice Inspector (also a Detective) and kills it, taking only 1.
# Burden of Proof has flash (CR 702.8a): it is cast on turn 1 in Bot1's own main phase here and then again as an instant in the next scenario.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Novice Inspector
Burden of Proof
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Novice Inspector
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Novice Inspector.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Burden of Proof.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Novice Inspector)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Power = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Toughness = 4
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Novice Inspector.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Novice Inspector > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Novice Inspector > Novice Inspector)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Burden of Proof.AttachedTo = Novice Inspector
Bot1.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Damage = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Novice Inspector
Bot1.Life = 20
